Many digital audio systems are being introduced into the consumer audio market,
including compact disc, digital audio tape, digital sound processors, and digital TV-sound.
The digital audio signals in these systems are being processed by a number of (V)LSI
ICs, such as:
• A/D and D/A converters;
• digital signal processors;
• error correction for compact disc and digital recording;
• digital filters;
• digital input/output interfaces.
Standardized communication structures are vital for both the equipment and the IC
manufacturer, because they increase system flexi…

As shown in Figure 1, the bus has three lines:
• Continuous Serial Clock (SCK);
• Word Select (WS);
• Serial Data (SD);
and the device generating SCK and WS is the controller.
